invariant: INV-7
file: suite.h
catches: webpki_session_aes_runtime
reason: an AES=runtime session whose caller's probe found no AES
  instructions takes the AES-first default order, so its client offers
  AES-256-GCM and AES-128-GCM and its server selects one of them, and the
  traffic keys then run the AES instructions the caller said the CPU
  lacks. test_webpki_runtime_answers requires the hello of the absent
  answer to list ChaCha20 alone.

--- old
    if (cfg->aes_instructions != CH_AES_INSTRUCTIONS_PRESENT) {
--- new
    if (cfg->aes_instructions == 0) {
